{"chunk_id": "c35a5cb3d31b", "text": "This section concludes the terrifying scope of Janamejaya\u2019s snake\u2011sacrifice by listing numerous serpent chiefs from different lineages\u2014Takshaka, Airavata, Kauravya, and Dhritarashtra\u2014who were dragged into the sacrificial fire by the power of Vedic mantras. The narrative emphasizes the immense scale of destruction: countless serpents of monstrous size and supernatural power perish under the curse driving the ritual. The focus then shifts to a decisive moment: as the serpent king Takshaka is pulled toward the fire, the sage Astika intervenes. By commanding Takshaka to \u201cStay,\u201d he suspends him in midair and persuades King Janamejaya to end the sacrifice. The ritual stops, the surviving serpents are saved, and they grant Astika a boon that anyone who remembers his deed will be protected from snakebite.\nAstika halts Takshaka midair and persuades King Janamejaya to end the snake\u2011sacrifice, saving the serpent race and receiving a boon protecting readers from snake harm.\nThemes: mercy over vengeance, power of vows and boons, ritual sacrifice, divine intervention, protection through remembrance", "vector": [0.0019986387342214584, -0.01721164584159851, -0.0013624741695821285, -0.002716363174840808, -0.01500009372830391, 0.016428673639893532, -0.020728150382637978, -0.0030357332434505224, 0.00012845633318647742, -0.024986419826745987, 0.012452000752091408, 0.000711285334546119, 0.020068805664777756, 0.03406614437699318, -0.009155277162790298, -0.0067514157854020596, 0.051428891718387604, -0.0052335490472614765, 0.014107231050729752, -0.00437846127897501, -0.009794017300009727, 0.005511709954589605, -0.007561860140413046, 0.030110077932476997, -0.01828308030962944, 0.02166222222149372, 0.0037259848322719336, -0.038269467651844025, -0.0034873157273977995, -0.009897039271891117, -0.016703400760889053, -0.007211583200842142, -0.007568728644400835, -0.00486266752704978, -0.040879376232624054, -0.0019196547800